<title>POLAND: Poland's Wroclaw looks for muni bond issue agent.</title>
<headline>Poland's Wroclaw looks for muni bond issue agent.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The city of Wroclaw in south-western Poland opened a tender for lead-managing its planned 50 million zloty municipal bond issue, the city said in an newspaper advertisement on Friday.</p>
<p>Preliminary bids must be entered by May 12, 1997 and will be judged on price, the value of the offer and the realibility of the agent.</p>
<p>Wroclaw officials want to hold the issue roughly around the turn of this year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
